# Two rounds of a fair coin that increments c on heads:
#   wp({c := c + 1}[1/2]{skip}, c) = 1/2 (c + 1) + 1/2 c = c + 1/2,
# so two rounds give c + 1 and, from c = 0, the expectation of c is 1.  The lower bound 1 is
# exact.  The choice inside the bounded loop is unrolled with it, giving a weighted sum of
# applications of the post-expectation, which no loop function wraps.
# Expected: valid.  Before the bounded loop was unrolled the run stopped with an assertion
# failure.
nat c;
c := 0;
loop(2) {
	{
		c := c + 1;
	}[1/2]{
		skip
	}
}
?Ex [c] >= 1
